# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# VITE_SITE_URL: Public canonical origin used by SEO, sitemap, and social previews.
VITE_SITE_URL="https://identra.awncorp.vn"

# VITE_IDENTRA_API_URL: Origin of the Identra API used by the sample university portal and the
# sample employer demo. Defaults to https://api-identra.awncorp.vn. Must be https, except plain http
# on 127.0.0.1 / localhost for local work, e.g. the development stand-in (npm run dev:api):
# VITE_IDENTRA_API_URL="http://127.0.0.1:47310"

# VITE_CERTNET_GATEWAY_URL and VITE_CERTNET_NETWORK: the CertNet gateway through which the web trial wallet
# checks issuers of the second trust path (ADR-0020: issuer identified on CertNet instead of by an X.509
# certificate). Set both or neither. Neither (the default) turns that path off: the site behaves exactly as
# without it, contacts no gateway, and the trial wallet refuses such issuers' documents. The URL is an
# origin with an optional path prefix, https, except plain http on 127.0.0.1 / localhost for local work
# (e.g. the fake gateway of e2e/certnet-fake); the network is local, testnet or mainnet. The gateway must
# answer CORS for this site on GET /v1/dids/* and /v1/trust-registry/issuers/*, and the Content-Security-
# Policy must list its origin in connect-src (deploy/nginx/identra-web.conf.example). Not deployed yet.
# A production build (npm run build) refuses the local network (anyone can write its register) and any gateway
# that is not https: the build fails.
# VITE_CERTNET_GATEWAY_URL="http://127.0.0.1:47480"
# VITE_CERTNET_NETWORK="local"

# VITE_CERTNET_ALLOW_LOCAL_FOR_TESTS: TEST-ONLY. Set to "true" only for an end-to-end test build against a local
# fake gateway (e2e): a production build then accepts VITE_CERTNET_NETWORK=local and a plain-http loopback
# gateway, and the site shows a "test build" marker wherever CertNet results appear. Never set it for a site
# anyone else will use.
# VITE_CERTNET_ALLOW_LOCAL_FOR_TESTS="true"

# IDENTRA_ROOT_CA_FILE: Optional path to the Identra Root CA certificate (PEM) whose SHA-256
# fingerprint the Security page publishes. Defaults to src/identra/trust/root-ca.pem. A production
# build fails when the file is missing; the dev server shows a "not configured" state instead.
# IDENTRA_ROOT_CA_FILE="src/identra/trust/root-ca.pem"
# For the product page in development, the API stand-in (npm run dev:api) signs real product chains
# with a throwaway PKI in .dev-identra/ (git-ignored); pin its root so the browser verification passes:
# IDENTRA_ROOT_CA_FILE=".dev-identra/root-ca.pem"
# Optional: IDENTRA_ROOT_CA_NEXT_FILE (second root during a rollover) and IDENTRA_EXPECTED_ROOT_SHA256
# (the build fails unless a published root has this SHA-256 fingerprint; set by the deploy script).
